card.statement:
Let $e_1,e_2,\dots,$ be a basis of a vector space $U$, $f_1,f_2,\dots,$ be a basis of $V$, and $g_1,g_2,\dots$ be a basis of $W$.

- [(a)] The composition of a linear mapping ${\mathcal
      A}: U\to V$ and a semilinear mapping ${\mathcal B}:
      V\dashrightarrow W$ is the semilinear mapping with matrix

\begin{equation}
(\mathcal B \mathcal
A)_{ge}=\mathcal B_{gf}
\mathcal A_{fe}
\end{equation}

- [(b)] The composition of a semilinear mapping ${\mathcal A}:
     U\dashrightarrow V$ and a linear mapping ${\mathcal B}:
     V\to W$ is the semilinear mapping with matrix

\begin{equation}
(\mathcal B \mathcal
A)_{ge}=\overline{\mathcal B}_{gf} \mathcal
A_{fe}
\end{equation}
